      "content": "While ibuprofen can help alleviate migraine symptoms, it's generally recommended to wait a few hours before taking medication to see if the aura symptoms pass. This allows you to avoid the use of painkillers during the migraine cycle, which can prolong its duration. If your symptoms subside on their own, taking ibuprofen and resting is a good option, but if they worsen or you experience severe symptoms, such as severe vomiting, sensitivity to light, or difficulty speaking, it's best to seek medical attention.",
